   "text": "The SMILES below was read region by region from the drawing. It describes a PROTAC-type molecule with a kinase-binding head, a long linker and a VHL-type E3-ligase ligand.\n\n- **Kinase-binding head:** an imidazo[1,2-a]pyrazine carries a cyclopropyl on the pyrazine carbon and a 1H-pyrazol-4-yl on the imidazole carbon. Its 8-NH is bonded to a 2-fluorophenyl ring.\n- **Linker:** the aryl ring has a para C(=O) joined to a piperazine nitrogen. The other piperazine nitrogen carries a chain of 9 CH2 groups ending in a C(=O) amide. I counted the zigzag vertices one at a time to get nine.\n- **VHL ligand:** the amide NH is attached to a tert-leucine whose \u03b1-carbon is drawn with a wedge. That carbon is bonded to a tert-butyl group and to a C(=O) that acylates a 4-hydroxyproline nitrogen. The hydroxyproline carboxamide is bonded to a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzylamine.\n- **Stereochemistry:** the three stereocentres (tert-leucine \u03b1-carbon, hydroxyproline C2 and C4) are written to match the wedges and hashes. They also match the usual VHL ligand configuration, (S)-tert-leucine and (2S,4R)-hydroxyproline. I checked each @/@@ by permutation against the standard VHL-ligand SMILES.\n\nSMILES: O=C(CCCCCCCCCN1CCN(CC1)C(=O)c1ccc(Nc2nc(C3CC3)cn3c(-c4cn[nH]c4)cnc23)c(F)c1)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)NCc1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
  }
